<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela bolivar softens to 475.50/476.50/dlr.</title>
<headline>Venezuela bolivar softens to 475.50/476.50/dlr.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Venezuelan bolivar slipped in busy trade to 475.50/476.50 in an unusual spurt of late holiday trade, brokers said.</p>
<p>On Thursday, the unit closed at 475.00/476.00 per dollar.</p>
<p>&quot;It's incredible, we were not expecting any kind of movement in the market over the holidays,&quot; said one trader. &quot;Everything should have been very quiet.&quot;</p>
<p>Traders attributed the dollar demand, principally from corporate clients, to low Venezuelan interest rates. One added: &quot;The Central Bank, as ever, was in the market&quot;.</p>
<p>((-- Ana Isabel Martinez, Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600))</p>
